{
  "id": "ep151",
  "duration": 48.849,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.579,
      "text": "A twelve-year cosmic voyage is hunting down a record eight asteroids.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Lucy-ArtistsConcept.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/SwRI",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lucy-ArtistsConcept.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 4.567,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.579,
      "end": 13.774,
      "text": "Launched on October sixteenth, 2021, the ambitious Lucy mission set out across the solar system with a unique cargo on board.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Atlas V rocket stands upright on launchpad for Lucy mission (6890383).jpeg",
        "credit": "U.S. Space Force photo by Joshua Conti",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Atlas_V_rocket_stands_upright_on_launchpad_for_Lucy_mission_(6890383).jpeg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.567,
          "end": 9.167,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 9.167,
          "end": 13.767,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 13.774,
      "end": 21.394,
      "text": "Named after famous hominin fossils, the spacecraft carries an actual disc made entirely of lab-grown diamonds.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Lucy blackbg.jpg",
        "credit": "120",
        "license": "CC BY 2.5",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lucy_blackbg.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 13.767,
          "end": 21.4,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 21.394,
      "end": 28.039,
      "text": "Its ultimate target is six Jupiter trojan asteroids trapped securely in the giant planet's orbit.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Illustration of Asteroid Belts (2021-005).tif",
        "credit": "ILLUSTRATION: NASA, ESA, Joseph Olmsted (STScI)",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Illustration_of_Asteroid_Belts_(2021-005).tif"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 21.4,
          "end": 23.933,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 23.933,
          "end": 28.033,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 28.039,
      "end": 35.459,
      "text": "Along the way, principal investigator Harold Levison guided the probe right past main-belt asteroid Dinkinesh.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Lucy - Asteroid Dinkinesh Flyby (SVS5155 - lucy dinkinesh withDates 00385 print).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA's Scientific Visualization Studio - SwRI/Katherine Kretke, Advocates in Manpower Management, Inc./David Ladd, KBR Wyle Services, LLC/Dan Gallagher",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lucy_-_Asteroid_Dinkinesh_Flyby_(SVS5155_-_lucy_dinkinesh_withDates_00385_print).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 28.033,
          "end": 35.467,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 35.459,
      "end": 42.859,
      "text": "High-resolution cameras revealed a tiny moon orbiting the rock that was actually a rare contact binary.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Lucy Sees Asteroid Dinkinesh in Detail (SVS14596 - Dinkinesh Detailed View VERTICAL Preview).png",
        "credit": "NASA's Scientific Visualization Studio - KBR Wyle Services, LLC/Dan Gallagher, SwRI/Harold Levison, Southwest Research Institute/John Spencer, London Stereoscopic Company/Brian May, Claudia Manzoni, N",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lucy_Sees_Asteroid_Dinkinesh_in_Detail_(SVS14596_-_Dinkinesh_Detailed_View_VERTICAL_Preview).png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 35.467,
          "end": 42.867,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 42.859,
      "end": 48.499,
      "text": "That surprising hidden moon officially started this record-breaking twelve-year cosmic voyage.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Lucy-ArtistsConcept.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/SwRI",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lucy-ArtistsConcept.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 42.867,
